%% Authentication & Authorization Flow: Cognito + JWT + IAM
sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Admin
    participant Cognito as Cognito<br/>(IdP)
    participant APIGateway as API Gateway
    participant IAM as IAM Policies
    participant Lambda as Lambda

    Admin->>Cognito: 1. POST /auth/login<br/>(email, password)
    Cognito->>Cognito: Validate credentials
    Cognito-->>Admin: 2. JWT token<br/>(expires: 1 hour)

    Admin->>APIGateway: 3. POST /posts<br/>Header: Authorization: Bearer JWT

    APIGateway->>Cognito: 4. Validate JWT signature<br/>& expiration
    Cognito-->>APIGateway: 5. ✓ Valid<br/>(claims: { userId: 1, ... })

    APIGateway->>IAM: 6. Check policy:<br/>User=1 can POST /posts?
    IAM-->>APIGateway: 7. ✓ Allowed<br/>(user:1 has PostsWrite)

    APIGateway->>Lambda: 8. Route to handler
    Lambda->>Lambda: 9. Execute business logic
    Lambda-->>APIGateway: 10. Success (201 Created)
    APIGateway-->>Admin: 11. Created post

    rect rgb(200, 220, 255)
        Note over Admin, IAM: If JWT invalid or IAM denies → 401/403 error
    end
